  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Mushroom placement, cap sizes, the leaves' paths and the circle's angle change per cast. Heal pulses every 1 s, always."
  },
  "director_notes": "Lisa asked for druid healing auras with leaves and mushrooms. Mushrooms are the new eruption shape `mushrooms` (two loose rings, smaller outer row) so they pop up with a springy overshoot and sink back at the end. Leaves and motes use the new sparks `orbit_hz` to swirl round the druid. The heal pulse runs inward (start radius bigger than end) to say life flows in. Loop 1200-4200 ms."
